From: sdolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: j314s: E4 - drive the dock tunnel from dcpext0

Opt-in experiment; apply after 0001 through 0014.

The 2026-10-17 macOS baseline on this MacBookPro18,3 (macOS 27.0.1,
WD22TB4 attached) shows macOS routing atc1-dpin0 to dispext0 port 0
(display-crossbar0 "ufp0,0-dfp1,1"), on DPTX port 0, and training a
4-lane HBR3 link to the dock HDMI sink about 90 ms after HPD. Linux has
only ever tried dcpext1 (dispext1,0), whose firmware answers the tunnel
connect with DEVICE_NOT_RESPONDING (E1).

Under ENABLE_DCPEXT0_TB_TUNNEL, give the tunnel role to dcpext0: ATC1
crossbar "dpin0" control with mux state 0 (dispext0,0), dptx-phy 1, the
same DP-IN tunnel PHY, and no HDMI GPIOs or Type-C mux graph. dcpext1
returns to its stock DP-altmode wiring and the NHI points at dcpext0.
The built-in HDMI port has no display controller while this is defined.

Validated offline only: applies after 0001-0014; t6000-j314s compiles
with stock dtc 1.6.1 with and without the define (Asahi float cells
integer-ized for the check), adding only the graph_child_address
warning dcpext1 already has. In the E4 DTB, dcpext0 mux-controls point
to mux@b0304c000 cell 1, dp-tunnel-phy to phy@e50000, and the NHI
dp-source to dcp@289c00000. Not booted.

Signed-off-by: sdolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
---
  arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6000-j314s.dts      |  6 +++
  arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-j314-j316.dtsi | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
  2 files changed, 58 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6000-j314s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6000-j314s.dts
index af6838d..dbfc45e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6000-j314s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6000-j314s.dts
@@ -18,6 +18,12 @@
  * PHY. See mseries/fairydust/usb4/DP-TUNNEL-RE.md.
  */
 #define ENABLE_DCPEXT_TB_TUNNEL
+/*
+ * E4 (experimental): use dcpext0 for the tunnel, as macOS does on this
+ * machine. Disables the built-in HDMI port. See
+ * mseries/fairydust/usb4/evidence/2026-10-17-macos-baseline-dcpext0.md.
+ */
+#define ENABLE_DCPEXT0_TB_TUNNEL
 
 #include "t600x-j314-j316.dtsi"
 
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-j314-j316.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-j314-j316.dtsi
index 9877b8d..a36a981 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-j314-j316.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t600x-j314-j316.dtsi
@@ -875,4 +875,56 @@
 &dpin1_0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+#ifdef ENABLE_DCPEXT0_TB_TUNNEL
+/*
+ * E4: drive the dock tunnel from dcpext0 instead of dcpext1.
+ *
+ * The 2026-10-17 macOS baseline (macOS 27.0.1, dock attached) shows macOS
+ * routing atc1-dpin0 to dispext0 port 0 (crossbar "ufp0,0-dfp1,1") and
+ * training a 4-lane HBR3 link to the dock HDMI sink within ~90 ms of HPD.
+ * Linux has only tried dcpext1 (dispext1,0), whose firmware answers
+ * DEVICE_NOT_RESPONDING. This swaps the tunnel role to the proven DCP.
+ *
+ * Cost: dcpext0 normally drives the built-in HDMI port (atcphy3). With this
+ * define the built-in HDMI has no display controller; dcpext1 returns to its
+ * stock Type-C DP-altmode wiring. Opt-in only: drop the define to revert.
+ */
+&dcpext0 {
+	apple,connector-type = "DP";
+	/delete-property/ hdmi-hpd-gpios;
+	/delete-property/ hdmi-pwren-gpios;
+	/delete-property/ dp2hdmi-pwren-gpios;
+	apple,dptx-phy = <1>;
+	phys = <&atcphy1 PHY_TYPE_DP>;
+	phy-names = "dp-phy";
+	apple,dp-tunnel-phy = <&dpin1_0>;
+	/* "dpin0" mux control of the ATC1 crossbar; state 0 = dispext0,0. */
+	mux-controls = <&atcphy1_xbar 1>;
+	mux-control-names = "dp-xbar";
+	mux-index = <0>;
+	apple,dp-tunnel;
+	/*
+	 * Drop only the HDMI DP-out endpoint (port@1) so no Type-C mux graph is
+	 * found; keep port@0, the dpaudio1 link.
+	 */
+	ports {
+		/delete-node/ port@1;
+	};
+};
+
+&atcphy3_dp {
+	/delete-property/ remote-endpoint;
+};
+
+&dcpext1 {
+	/delete-property/ apple,dp-tunnel;
+	/delete-property/ apple,dp-tunnel-phy;
+	mux-controls = <&atcphy1_xbar 0>;
+};
+
+&usb4_1_nhi {
+	apple,dp-source = <&dcpext0>;
+};
+#endif /* ENABLE_DCPEXT0_TB_TUNNEL */
 #endif
-- 
